  {
   "id": "mPYGE8qJBAAJ",
   "from": "Chris Sutherland",
   "author": "58a62321f08f30f8",
   "date": "2020-12-19T10:18:30Z",
   "subject": "Re: [oscr] oSCR.parfit() iteration limit error",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi Clay,<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Not sure what’s happening there. Trouble with the parfit function is that there is lot happening n the fly in terms of function calls, despite its ultimate function being quite straightforward. Personally, I have started directly running models in parallel (i.e., just writing the few lines of code parfit needs to, just without all the generalization and automation). So, here is a short script that mirrors the parfit workflow, but at the end does the parallelization directly. Grey is just setting up the bear data, blue is what you want to focus on!<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">library(oSCR)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">data(beardata)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">#create the ‘time’ time varying covariate<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">beardata$tdf$sep &lt;- &#39;/&#39;<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">beardata$tdf$rand1 &lt;- rnorm(nrow(beardata$tdf))<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">beardata$tdf$rand2 &lt;- rnorm(nrow(beardata$tdf))<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">#create scrframe<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">data &lt;-data2oscr(edf=beardata$edf,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                 tdf=list(beardata$tdf),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                 sess.col=which(colnames(beardata$edf)%in%&quot;Session&quot;),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                 id.col=which(colnames(beardata$edf)%in%&quot;ID&quot;),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                 occ.col=which(colnames(beardata$edf)%in%&quot;Occasion&quot;),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                 trap.col=which(colnames(beardata$edf)%in%&quot;trapID&quot;),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                 sex.col=which(colnames(beardata$edf)%in%&quot;Sex&quot;),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                 sex.nacode=&quot;NA&quot;,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                 K=8,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                 tdf.sep = &quot;/&quot;,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                 trapcov.names = c(&quot;rand1&quot;,&quot;rand2&quot;),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                 ntraps=nrow(beardata$tdf))<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">bear.sf &lt;-data$scrFrame<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">bear.ss &lt;-make.ssDF(scrFrame = bear.sf, buffer = 2, res = 1)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">(mods &lt;- make.mods(density = c(~1),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                   detection = c(~1,~rand1,~rand2),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#a6a6a6\">                   sigma = c(~1)))<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">library(foreach)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">library(doParallel)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">cl &lt;- makeCluster(3)    #make the cluster<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">registerDoParallel(cl)  #register the cluster<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">out2 &lt;- foreach(i=1:3,.packages = &quot;oSCR&quot;) %dopar% {<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">  <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">  m &lt;- list(mods[i,1][[1]], </span><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:red\"># <i>i</i>th model</span></b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">            mods[i,2][[1]],<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">            mods[i,3][[1]],<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">            mods[i,4][[1]]) </span><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:red\">#this is a bit clumsy, but its morning here</span></b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:red\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,sans-serif;color:#0000cc\">☹</span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">  <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">  out &lt;- oSCR.fit(m, bear.sf,bear.ss, trimS=2)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">  return(out)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">}<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:#0000cc\">stopCluster(cl)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"> Hope that helps. Actually, probably better from a #learnR perspective to be able to do this rather than rely on the wrapper <span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,sans-serif\">😊</span> <u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Chris<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div></div></div></div>"
    ],
