     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Hi Clay,<u></u><u></u></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Not sure what’s happening there. Trouble with the parfit function is that there is lot happening n the fly in terms of function calls, despite its ultimate function being quite straightforward. Personally, I have started directly running models in parallel (i.e., just writing the few lines of code parfit needs to, just without all the generalization and automation). So, here is a short script that mirrors the parfit workflow, but at the end does the parallelization directly. Grey is just setting up the bear data, blue is what you want to focus on!<u></u><u></u></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">library(oSCR)<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">data(beardata)<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">#create the ‘time’ time varying covariate<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">beardata$tdf$sep &lt;- &#39;/&#39;<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">beardata$tdf$rand1 &lt;- rnorm(nrow(beardata$tdf))<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">beardata$tdf$rand2 &lt;- rnorm(nrow(beardata$tdf))<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">#create scrframe<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">data &lt;-data2oscr(edf=beardata$edf,<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                 tdf=list(beardata$tdf),<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                 sess.col=which(colnames(beardata$edf)%in%&quot;Session&quot;),<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                 id.col=which(colnames(beardata$edf)%in%&quot;ID&quot;),<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                 occ.col=which(colnames(beardata$edf)%in%&quot;Occasion&quot;),<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                 trap.col=which(colnames(beardata$edf)%in%&quot;trapID&quot;),<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                 sex.col=which(colnames(beardata$edf)%in%&quot;Sex&quot;),<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                 sex.nacode=&quot;NA&quot;,<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                 K=8,<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                 tdf.sep = &quot;/&quot;,<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                 trapcov.names = c(&quot;rand1&quot;,&quot;rand2&quot;),<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                 ntraps=nrow(beardata$tdf))<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">bear.sf &lt;-data$scrFrame<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">bear.ss &lt;-make.ssDF(scrFrame = bear.sf, buffer = 2, res = 1)<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">(mods &lt;- make.mods(density = c(~1),<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                   detection = c(~1,~rand1,~rand2),<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">                   sigma = c(~1)))<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">library(foreach)<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">library(doParallel)<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">cl &lt;- makeCluster(3)    #make the cluster<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">registerDoParallel(cl)  #register the cluster<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">out2 &lt;- foreach(i=1:3,.packages = &quot;oSCR&quot;) %dopar% {<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\"> <span> </span><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">  m &lt;- list(mods[i,1][[1]],<span> </span></span><b><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:red\">#<span> </span><i>i</i>th model</span></b><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\"><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">            mods[i,2][[1]],<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">            mods[i,3][[1]],<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">            mods[i,4][[1]])<span> </span></span><b><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:red\">#this is a bit clumsy, but its morning here</span></b><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:red\"><span> </span></span><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">☹</span><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\"><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\"> <span> </span><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">  out &lt;- oSCR.fit(m, bear.sf,bear.ss, trimS=2)<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">  return(out)<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">}<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&quot;Fira Code&quot;;color:rgb(0,0,204)\">stopCluster(cl)<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Hope that helps. Actually, probably better from a #learnR perspective to be able to do this rather than rely on the wrapper<span> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,sans-serif\">😊</span><u></u><u></u></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Chris<u></u><u></u></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div><div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">On Fri, 18 Dec 2020, 20:03 Clayton Lamb, &lt;<a href style=\"color:blue;text-decoration:underline\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ctl...@ualberta.ca</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></div></div><blockquote style=\"border-style:none none none solid;border-left-width:1pt;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);padding:0cm 0cm 0cm 6pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-right:0cm\" type=\"cite\"><div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Has anyone run into the following error with oSCR.parfit(). It is thrown within a few minutes of the models starting up.<u></u><u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">&quot;Error in { : task 1 failed - &quot;invalid iteration limit in nlm””<u></u><u></u></div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">The call:<u></u><u></u></div></div><div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">dens.mods &lt;- oSCR.parfit( mods=mods.d, <u></u><u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">                          scrFrame=ms.sf,                      <u></u><u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">                          ssDF=ms.ssDF,<u></u><u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">                          trimS=35E3,<u></u><u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">                          ncores=6)<u></u><u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div></div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span>Best,<br>Clayton<br><br>--<br>Clayton Lamb, PhD (he/him)<u></u><u></u></span></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span>Postdoctoral Researcher | Liber Ero Fellow<br>Universities of British Columbia &amp; Montana<br>Residing in Fernie, BC | Ktunaxa Nation Territory<br>e:<span> </span><a href style=\"color:blue;text-decoration:underline\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ctl...@ualberta.ca</a><br>p: <a href=\"tel:(778)%20215-0334\" value=\"+17782150334\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">778-215-0334</a><br>t: <a href=\"https://twitter.com/ClaytonTLamb\" style=\"color:blue;text-decoration:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://twitter.com/ClaytonTLamb&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492054673000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3UIpxG-D_mWpmKO7WBp1qv\">@ClaytonTLamb</a><br>w: <a href=\"http://www.lamb-eco-research.ca/\" style=\"color:blue;text-decoration:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.lamb-eco-research.ca/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492054673000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2UavdItgMIVQ89g0EAGvRk\">www.lamb-eco-research.ca</a><u></u><u></u></span></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span><u></u> <u></u></span></div></div></div></div></div></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span><u></u> <u></u></span></div></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 12pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div></div></div><div style=\"margin:0cm;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">--<span> </span><br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;oSCR&quot; group.<br>To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to<span> </span><a href style=\"color:blue;text-decoration:underline\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_package...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>To view this discussion on the web visit<span> </span><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/oscr_package/86056A41-F07B-49B7-A816-57F5989E87E3%40ualberta.ca?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" style=\"color:blue;text-decoration:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/oscr_package/86056A41-F07B-49B7-A816-57F5989E87E3%2540ualberta.ca?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492054673000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1a6bklAdTLkL-rmelSotU7\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/oscr_package/86056A41-F07B-49B7-A816-57F5989E87E3%40ualberta.ca</a>.<u></u><u></u></div></blockquote></div></div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><br></div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-c